  nonce: e74e  # e74e
  data:  # e74e
    kind: invariant  # e74e
    title: "META: Sketch budget enforcement layered without coordinator"  # e74e
    status: violated  # e74e
    priority: 1  # e74e
    parent:  # e74e
    tags:  # e74e
    - dogfood_corpus_20260528  # e74e
    - dogfood_umbrella  # e74e
    - dogfood_severity_significant  # e74e
    - sketch_pipeline  # e74e
    isbefore: []  # e74e
    duplicate_of: []  # e74e
    not_duplicate_of: []  # e74e
    pr_ref:  # e74e
    description: "**Origin.** Filed 2026-05-30 from the unlinked-investigation G3 sub-agent (notebookjournal_05302026_0411_unlinked_G3_sketch.md Theme B). Three sketch-pipeline items fail in three different sites at three different stages of budget enforcement.\n\n**The shape.** `sketch` accepts a `-t/--budget` flag (target node/edge count). Budget enforcement is layered across three components (compact projection, multi-resolution generation, centrality computation), each implemented independently. Symptoms:\n\n1. **`nodes_summary` reports pre-shrink counts.** `compact.py:1448` writes `nodes_summary` from the input arrays before the projection loop at 1478-1517 mutates `nodes`/`edges` to the budget target. Result: the JSON envelope's summary contradicts its own arrays. (INV-pazur)\n\n2. **Multi-resolution comparison sketches always run.** `cli.py:798-841` unconditionally generates the 4x and 16x comparison sketches; there's no opt-out for batch use. On a corpus of repos this is wasted work. (WI-fufop)\n\n3. **Budget ≥ 16146 crashes via SIGPIPE.** `ranking.py:_compute_centrality_with_python` opens a subprocess but doesn't handle the early-exit case; budget ≥ 16146 causes exit 141 with 0 bytes output. (INV-vopuh)\n\n**Shared root: no budget-enforcement coordinator.** No single component owns \"given budget B, here is the pipeline that produces a single sketch of size ≤B with a self-consistent summary, no wasted comparison sketches, and graceful failure on resource-exhaustion.\" Each component does its piece in isolation.\n\n**Members at filing time.** INV-pazur (P1), WI-fufop (P1), INV-vopuh (P1).\n\n**Adjacent cluster (in linked-bucket).** WI-ribag (warm-cache sketch slow), WI-zipoj (>1M-LOC warm sketch 14-22 min), INV-jumim (sketch --input re-walks filesystem) — these are sketch-performance hot-path items, not budget-coordination items, but share substrate with this META.\n\n**Fix shape.** Single `SketchBudget` coordinator that wraps the three components: (a) pre-shrink summary lazy-evaluation, (b) `--no-comparisons` opt-out wired through to comparison generation, (c) SIGPIPE handler in the centrality subprocess path. Each member item is one fix-site.\n\n**Cross-cluster note.** INV-pazur ↔ INV-titid: both share the \"compact-shrink without reconciliation\" pattern. INV-titid lives in slice-projection territory (G2) but the architectural fix is parallel — finalize-after-shrink hook that re-derives metadata from the post-shrink arrays."  # e74e
    fields:  # e74e
      statement: "For a given sketch budget B, the pipeline must produce one sketch of size ≤B with a self-consistent summary, with no wasted secondary work (comparison sketches) unless explicitly requested, and with graceful failure on resource exhaustion."  # e74e
      root_cause: "Budget enforcement is layered without a coordinator. Three independent failure sites: compact.py:1448 writes nodes_summary before the projection loop at 1478-1517 mutates the arrays; cli.py:798-841 unconditionally generates the 4x and 16x comparison sketches with no opt-out for batch use; ranking.py:_compute_centrality_with_python subprocess exits early with SIGPIPE at budget ≥ 16146 and has no handler."  # e74e
- op: discuss  # 8696
  at: '2026-06-02T08:02:26Z'  # 8696
  by: agent  # 8696
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 8696
  clock: 2  # 8696
  nonce: '8696'  # 8696
  message: "Pass-32 face: `hypergumbo compact` violates monotonicity — `compact --max-symbols N` is NOT a subset of `compact --max-symbols M` for N<M (F32.9, F32.13).\n\nINV-fanur's scope: \"For a given sketch budget B, the pipeline must produce one sketch of size ≤B with a self-consistent summary, with no wasted secondary work… and graceful failure on resource exhaustion.\" Pass-32 surfaces a fourth budget-coordination face — selection across two budget values is not monotonic.\n\n**Repro.**\n```\n$ hypergumbo compact --input bm.json --max-symbols 50  --out /tmp/p32_comp50.json\n$ hypergumbo compact --input bm.json --max-symbols 200 --out /tmp/p32_comp200.json\n\ncompact-50 nodes: 50           compact-200 nodes: 200\ncompact-50 ⊂ compact-200?  False  — 15 of 50 nodes (30%) in -50 are NOT in -200\ncompact-50 edges: 158          compact-200 edges: 800\ncompact-50 edges ⊂ -200?   False  — 61 of 158 edges (39%) in -50 are NOT in -200\n```\n\nA larger budget should never drop a node the smaller budget kept. 30% of the smaller selection vanishes under a 4× larger budget; this is a strict monotonicity violation in the connectivity-aware selection algorithm at `compact.py:format_tiered_behavior_map`. INV-pazur is the existing budget-coordination face about the `nodes_summary` post-shrink reconciliation gap; pass-32 supplies a sibling face about the selection algorithm itself.\n\n**Consumer impact.** A user testing with `--max-symbols 50` to scope a behavior map for an LLM context window, then later raising the budget to `--max-symbols 200` to get richer context, may find that previously-included central symbols disappear from the larger view. The \"compact form\" is not stable under budget change — adjacent-budget views are not subset-related. For agentic consumers comparing the 4k / 16k / 64k tiers (which are derived via this same selection path), the same non-monotonicity applies: tiered emissions don't form a containment chain.\n\n**Smaller secondary face — F32.13.** Of the 370 edges in the default compact (`--max-symbols 100`), the induced-subgraph invariant **holds** (370/370 intra-included endpoints, 0 dangling). However, the converse direction has a 2-edge gap: the substrate has 2 edges whose BOTH endpoints are in the compact's 100-node set but those edges are not in the compact's 370-edge list. Tiny but real edge-selection drop. Plausibly explained by edge dedup at the (src, dst, type) triplet level if the substrate has near-duplicates, but the substrate itself satisfies edge-triplet uniqueness (verified pass-24 NULL finding A.6). Worth a probe at the compact edge-selection step specifically.\n\n**Root cause hypothesis.** The connectivity-aware selection ranks nodes by centrality coverage; when the budget grows, the ranking may re-balance based on a different starting state (different greedy seed) producing a non-superset selection. The deterministic fix is either (a) lexicographic tie-break + monotonic seed, or (b) materialize the full ranking once and slice the prefix at the requested budget. Option (b) makes monotonicity by construction.\n\n**Fix-path candidate.** Extending INV-fanur's `SketchBudget` coordinator concept: the coordinator owns \"given budget B, produce a selection that is a prefix of the canonical ranking\" rather than independently re-running a budget-dependent greedy. This subsumes both the F32.9 monotonicity face and the existing INV-pazur post-shrink-summary face.\n\n**No status change.** Pass-32 supplies a fourth budget-coordination face under INV-fanur joining INV-pazur (post-shrink summary), WI-fufop (always-comparison sketches), and INV-vopuh (SIGPIPE >=16146).\n\nProbe artifacts: `/tmp/p32_outputD.log` section \"D.5\" (induced-subgraph invariant), section \"D.8\" (monotonicity check)."  # 8696
- op: discuss  # c369
  at: '2026-06-02T22:16:17Z'  # c369
  by: agent  # c369
  actor: jgstern_agent  # c369
  clock: 3  # c369
  nonce: c369  # c369
  message: "Pass 38 (2026-06-02, dogfooding) — 5 findings batched at compact algorithm characterization:\n\nF38.C1: --coverage value is SILENTLY IGNORED at the cardinality level. Tested cov=0.1/0.5/0.8/0.9/0.99 on /tmp/hg-dogfood-s21/bm.json with default --max-symbols=100; ALL 5 substrates produce IDENTICAL counts (100 nodes / 370 edges / 33 EPs / 16 features / 8 UCs) and BYTE-IDENTICAL file sizes (584496). SHA256 hashes differ — content differs in ordering/internal layout — but the symbol-selection cardinality is dominated by --max-symbols. --coverage flag's documented 'target centrality coverage 0.0-1.0' effect is not observable in top-level counts at default --max-symbols. Either coverage operates within the 100-node window (re-ranking) or is a no-op on this substrate at default budget. INV-fanur scope extends: 5th budget-coordination face joining INV-pazur / WI-fufop / INV-vopuh / pass-32 F32.9.\n\nF38.C2: --max-symbols 50→100→200→500 catastrophically violates containment monotonicity ACROSS ALL TRANSITIONS. Generalizes pass-32 F32.9 (15 of 50 in -50 not in -200) across full ms range:\n- ms_50 → ms_100: 12 lost (24%), 62 added\n- ms_100 → ms_200: 30 lost (30%), 130 added\n- ms_200 → ms_500: 52 lost (26%), 352 added\nLoss rate ~25-30% per doubling — roughly constant. Compact selection is NOT a top-N truncation of a stable ranking; connectivity-aware selection re-derives ranking per budget. Consumer impact: tiered compact emissions (4k/16k/64k) NEVER form containment chain. Pass-32 F32.9 fix-path (materialize single canonical ranking, slice prefix at requested budget) still valid; now sharply confirmed by 4-data-point sweep.\n\nF38.C3: --no-connectivity vs default at same params (cov=0.8, ms=100) produces 61/100 shared nodes (39 conn-only, 39 noconn-only). Algorithm choice (connectivity-aware) changes 39% of selected nodes at identical budget. --no-connectivity --help 'may produce disconnected subgraphs' understates: consumer choice changes WHICH 100 nodes, not how many.\n\nF38.C4: features=16 PRESERVED across ALL 10 compact variants (5 cov + 4 ms + 1 noconn) including ms_50 with only 50 nodes. Compact does NOT apply pass-37 F37.B1 EP-truncation logic to features array. Separate code path. The compact substrate has 100 nodes + 16 features + 33 EPs at default; features references can include node_ids OUTSIDE the 100-node window. Consumer expectation: feature.entry_nodes resolve to substrate nodes. With compact dropping 99.7% of root nodes but preserving 100% of features, feature.entry_nodes resolution rate could be substantially below 100% on compact substrates — to verify next pass.\n\nF38.C5: Edge density super-linear in --max-symbols. ms_100 = 3.7 edges/node, ms_200 = 4.0 e/n, ms_500 = 8.86 e/n. 2.5× node growth from ms_200 to ms_500 produces 5.5× edge growth. Selection prefers densely-connected nodes as budget expands; small budgets get a sparser graph than the per-symbol average would predict."  # c369
- op: discuss  # e3b6
  at: '2026-06-02T22:51:36Z'  # e3b6
  by: agent  # e3b6
  actor: jgstern_agent  # e3b6
  clock: 4  # e3b6
  nonce: e3b6  # e3b6
  message: "Pass 39 (2026-06-02, dogfooding) — 2 findings batched at compact --coverage characterization:\n\nF39.B1 (HEADLINE — UPGRADES pass-38 F38.C1 from 'silently ignored' to 'structurally dead-code'): --coverage flag is structurally dead-code in the DEFAULT connectivity-aware compact path. Code reading compact.py:\n- Default (connectivity_aware=True at compact.py:1046): calls select_by_connectivity(symbols, edges, seed_ids, max_additional, centrality) at line 1050. Function signature has NO target_coverage parameter. The flag value is stored in CompactConfig.target_coverage (default 0.8) but never read by the connectivity-aware selector.\n- --no-connectivity: calls select_by_coverage(symbols, edges, config, force_include_ids) at line 1071. This IS coverage-aware (at_coverage = coverage >= config.target_coverage at line 905).\n\nThe documented '--coverage / Target centrality coverage 0.0-1.0 (default: 0.8)' help text only takes effect when --no-connectivity is also set. Default-mode users see no behavioral change from --coverage. F38.C1 framing 'silently ignored at cardinality' was understated — flag is structurally inert in default path. Documentation/wiring gap: --help should either gate --coverage on --no-connectivity or wire --coverage through to select_by_connectivity (e.g., stop-condition at frontier expansion).\n\nF39.B2: Empirical verification of F39.B1 — --no-connectivity coverage sweep on /tmp/hg-dogfood-s21/bm.json:\n- cov=0.1 → 57 nodes / actual_coverage=0.1009 (stops at coverage 10.1%, before max-symbols 100)\n- cov=0.5 → 100 nodes / actual_coverage=0.1966 (max-symbols hit; coverage 50% UNREACHABLE)\n- cov=0.8 → 100 nodes / actual_coverage=0.1966 (max-symbols hit)\n- cov=0.99 → 100 nodes / actual_coverage=0.1966 (max-symbols hit)\n\nRoot substrate centrality is heavily distributed — top-100 nodes cover only 19.66% of total centrality. To make --coverage ≥0.5 actually trigger, user would need --max-symbols >> 100. No documented relationship between --coverage and --max-symbols in --help. 6th budget-coordination face joining INV-pazur / WI-fufop / INV-vopuh / pass-32 F32.9 / pass-38 F38.C1."  # e3b6
